WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:03.150
You're supposed to die to Genichiro at the start of the game

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:05.080
But what if... you don't?

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:11.759
That thought was teasing me for weeks after the game's release, and as I got good against him my mind began to race

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:13.299
with ideas.

00:00:13.299 --> 00:00:17.399
Maybe he won't cut my arm off and maybe I'll go through the game without a prosthetic arm!

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:21.449
What if I'm able to turn his bow into a prosthetic weapon?

00:00:21.449 --> 00:00:25.560
I thought maybe the credits will roll right here and now, game over!

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:29.140
What if it's just... Oh! Oh.

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:36.680
At least there's a little bit of lore here. The Ashina combat style is all about victory at any cost and

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:40.919
Genichiro using the ancient samurai cutscene technique is

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:44.100
definitely in keeping with that ethos.

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:51.000
The divine heir is coming with me.

00:00:51.129 --> 00:00:58.709
As you head into the Ashina outskirts still thinking about how you totally beat Genichiro and it isn't fair...

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:06.959
Remember to head upwards and to the left as soon as you arrive at the cannon section. There's a memorial mob merchant up here

00:01:06.959 --> 00:01:13.140
who sells firecrackers for 500 Sen and it is one of the strongest prosthetic tools in the game.

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:18.299
And as soon as you clear the cannon section, double back here before you fight the ogre.

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:23.100
There's a merchant tucked away and he's in a nook that you wouldn't really think to visit.

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:26.459
Anayama, dressed in patches and tatters,

00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:31.529
will trade information for 150 Sen before he upgrades his wares.

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:34.829
His prized possession is the Phantom Kunai.

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:37.740
It's this shuriken upgrade that you can purchase for

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:45.140
3,000 Sen. And it takes a little while for you to work towards this and one shuriken now costs two spirit emblems,

00:01:45.310 --> 00:01:49.229
but it's the best method you have, really, to do damage to enemies at a distance...

00:01:49.509 --> 00:01:50.920
And this is

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:58.920
kind of good against bosses that require a little bit more health damage before their posture begins to fall. And Anayama's

00:01:59.110 --> 00:02:01.110
ambitions have only just begun.

00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:12.740
The Ashina are low on salt, having used it all up during their constant warfare.

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:17.899
You can get this information on the bridge by the lake at the back of Ashina castle.

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:22.000
Next, he needs an assistant to help him loot the battlefield.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:29.690
The perfect companion for Anayama to

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:36.739
manipulate is Kotaro, a gentle giant found early on in Senpou Temple. Give Kotaro the red-and-white

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:39.500
pinwheel, and he'll come around to the idea.

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:48.709
This unlocks a few more sugars and an infinite store of black gunpowder and scrap iron,

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:51.410
but for the ending to their quest line,

00:02:51.410 --> 00:02:55.900
I'm gonna keep you around till the end of the video because it contains spoilers.

00:02:56.100 --> 00:03:02.100
To the right of the cannon bearer is a hidden drop down to a ledge containing a bunch of good items.

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:06.199
More interesting though, is this bit of snakeskin hanging from a tree.

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:11.400
It's a great little piece of environmental storytelling and it tells you that the snake really gets around this area.

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:16.610
A couple of tips in these videos are going to be lifted from popular speedrunning strats.

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:21.169
The most useful one I've found so far, is this way of dealing with the chained ogre.

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:25.909
So you crush a Guchin sugar, walk up to this brazier, and then take a sharp left.

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:30.350
This enables a backstab while he's still chained, and it's a good idea

00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:33.379
no matter how experienced you are, because let's be honest...

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:37.369
We've all been hit by this grab attack. After you defeat the ogre

00:03:37.370 --> 00:03:45.230
You can actually take a fairly pointless shortcut to Headless if you like. This gap in the wall enables a wall jump to this ledge

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:48.049
allowing you to open this door from behind and

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:51.259
enabling you to die to Headless faster.

00:03:51.510 --> 00:03:55.880
If you didn't know all headless enemies drop spiritful consumables,

00:03:55.880 --> 00:04:01.009
which are infinite use versions of the sugar items that consume three spirit emblems.

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:05.929
They don't last quite as long, but if you have two divine confetti handy,

00:04:05.930 --> 00:04:10.750
then you have a shot at beating this Headless which drops my favourite sugar, Ako.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:15.399
And while we're here, did you know that Sekiro actually has a passive ability called Night Eye?

00:04:15.829 --> 00:04:20.949
It's explained in one of the loading screens, and you can actually see it activate when you're in a dark place.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:23.240
And speaking of eyes...

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:27.400
After this encounter, look to the right of the first idol you come across.

00:04:27.770 --> 00:04:33.000
You'll find a small Senpou assassin who dreams of marrying the great serpent.

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:37.740
This is weird... So, kill him! (oh, ok?) 
And you'll receive the herb catalogue scrap,

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:40.820
which details where exactly to offer oneself.

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:48.320
This explains the palanquin within the valley, as there are two examples in the game of these being used for marriage

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:54.420
Them being used in this really formal ceremony might explain why the snake briefly stops

00:04:54.430 --> 00:04:57.459
its aggression towards us when it spots us going inside?

00:04:57.680 --> 00:05:03.730
In an earlier video we talked about what happens if you don't take the second death blow on main bosses

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:09.560
So maybe something will happen to you if you don't take a second death blow on the snake later on?

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:10.620
Hmm...

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:14.260
Your first death blow on Gyoubu refills a resurrection,

00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:17.740
which you can use to get an extra line of dialogue out of him.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:20.980
Quite a few main bosses react in this way!

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:23.560
Astonished that you're still able to stand, he says:

00:05:31.960 --> 00:05:37.720
A third resurrection is possible with a Jizo statue, and while Gyoubu says nothing here,

00:05:37.720 --> 00:05:42.160
this technique will be used in our next video, which is about Ashina castle,

00:05:42.160 --> 00:05:46.600
which reveals a fascinating little piece of lore about a character here, so

00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:50.860
subscribe and click the notification bell thing as well, so you don't miss it.

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:56.109
After Gyoubu, go up the staircase and have a chat with the guy in the tengu mask.

00:05:56.120 --> 00:06:02.360
He gives you a task to kill rats, vermin that he says are creeping about Ashina's lands.

00:06:02.700 --> 00:06:07.360
Senpou assassins count as rats, and there's a group of them to the right of the castle gate.

00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:12.320
Go up there, kill them, then go back and you receive the Ashina skill tree

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:16.420
which includes honestly probably the most powerful abilities in Sekiro.

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:17.060
Uh

00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:22.360
You've got deflection enhancements, you've got enhancements to combat, and it also contains, at the end

00:06:22.540 --> 00:06:30.400
what is arguably the best combat art in the game: ichimonji double. But we'll talk about combat arts in another video.

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:36.640
Above the tengu, accessible with a few ledge hangs, is a set of prayer beads which you might have missed.

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:37.940
And I should also mention,

00:06:37.940 --> 00:06:43.380
there's a gourd seed around the corner at the memorial mob. Just remember, you have to scroll down!

00:06:43.620 --> 00:06:48.760
I appreciate how gimmicky and well presented the Blazing Bull fight is, right?

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:53.740
But this fight probably is one of the less enjoyable fights in the game?

00:06:54.139 --> 00:06:59.978
Luckily if you want to skip it, you can! Only do this on New Game+, because you do miss out on a prayer bead.

00:07:00.050 --> 00:07:06.039
So: you hop up to this guard tower, you ledge jump at an angle off this wall, and you grapple onto the ledge.

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:10.839
Go to the top of the roof, run off at this exact angle as late as you can and

00:07:11.140 --> 00:07:14.200
sort of curve your character around the tree.

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:17.320
Take your second jump right here... and pray!

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:22.960
You don't want, after doing this like for 20 minutes:
"I think I'll just fight the bull next time!"

00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:29.400
To reward your prayer and your devotion, you arrive at this old woman right after the skip actually.

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:35.560
Show her how devoted you are by consuming all of your important items in front of her.

00:07:35.560 --> 00:07:39.140
As a reward for praying, you get other items of...

00:07:39.650 --> 00:07:41.650
equal value!
*laughs*

00:07:41.720 --> 00:07:49.104
The third prayer does net you some divine confetti, which is a pretty rare item this early in the game, so it's worth it for that.

00:07:49.104 --> 00:07:53.080
On the bridge opposite this woman, are two really nondescript soldiers.

00:07:53.180 --> 00:07:57.940
It's easy to run past them, but don't, because one of them actually drops the Gatehouse Key

00:07:57.940 --> 00:08:01.389
which you can use in the reservoir to loot Gyoubu's broken horn

00:08:01.759 --> 00:08:05.019
So before some of you type 
"I learned nothing new from this video!!1"

00:08:05.570 --> 00:08:11.199
Did you know that the horn itself is from Gyoubu's own helmet? It was snapped off during the rebellion.

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:14.380
And that its description reveals that after he was defeated,

00:08:14.540 --> 00:08:20.500
Ishiin Ashina was so impressed by Gyoubu's strength that he awarded him with the spear of none other than

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:22.080
Shuzen Tamura (?),

00:08:22.159 --> 00:08:26.199
The same general that we see Ishiin defeat in the opening cutscene.

00:08:27.030 --> 00:08:29.579
As we talked about in the Hirata Estates video,

00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:35.640
this is Inosuke, a man blinded and crippled during his fight with Lady Butterfly.

00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:42.540
Years later, his mother gives us the means to travel back to the Hirata Estates, talking about the divine Prince endlessly...

00:08:42.880 --> 00:08:47.880
But did you know that when you kill Lady Butterfly, both her and her son die?

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:53.399
The events of the past have been resolved.

00:08:54.640 --> 00:09:00.360
The following four facts are really good! But they take place after acquiring the mortal blade.

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:05.720
And, after completing the final sequence of the game as always. I have an escape route!

00:09:05.730 --> 00:09:12.300
You can go click the merch link down below and it'll evacuate you from this video to a safer place that's spoiler free!

00:09:12.540 --> 00:09:16.880
Because you shouldn't continue watching if you have not finished the game!

00:09:17.140 --> 00:09:18.920
During the siege of Ashina castle,

00:09:18.920 --> 00:09:24.800
You can take a shinobi kite to the Ashina outskirts, unlocking an invaluable section of the game.

00:09:24.800 --> 00:09:30.840
Herein, at the outskirts wall stairway, is probably the best farming location in the game!

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:34.380
So from the statue, simply head backwards towards the bridge,

00:09:34.780 --> 00:09:41.040
backstabbing all the way, and you'll receive a boatload of XP, gold, and rare upgrade materials!

00:09:41.710 --> 00:09:44.879
17: Maybe it's best if you did miss this one, honestly...

00:09:45.130 --> 00:09:50.010
When we left Anayama, he was overjoyed with the companion we brought him, but

00:09:50.200 --> 00:09:54.689
now during the siege of Ashina castle, he's bitten off more than he could chew

00:10:30.559 --> 00:10:34.599
The purpose of this quest line is to give you the Promissory Note.

00:10:34.700 --> 00:10:40.960
It only costs 1 Sen, but it discounts the cost of all items by 10%,

00:10:40.960 --> 00:10:46.440
which is a nice boost because you're going to want to clear out merchant stock before New Game+

00:10:46.560 --> 00:10:51.600
And it carries over into the beyond. A Sen saved is a Sen earned.

00:10:51.860 --> 00:10:55.880
Unfortunately, this is the end of Anayama and Kotaro.

00:10:56.400 --> 00:11:02.860
After you acquire the mortal blade, don't forget to give a merciful death to Hanbei the Undying.

00:11:02.860 --> 00:11:06.459
And as he prepares for death, he reveals the name of a close friend...

00:11:11.120 --> 00:11:19.240
Sekijo is the sculptor! A man who Hanbei understandably would have become close to, after all of his immortal years...

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:24.460
For, just as Sekiro translates roughly to "one-armed Wolf",

00:11:24.600 --> 00:11:28.880
Sekijo would translate roughly to "one-armed Orangutan".

00:11:29.020 --> 00:11:35.980
That's because "-ro" translates to "wolf", and there's something called a "shoujo" which is a sort of Japanese monkey spirit?

00:11:35.980 --> 00:11:42.320
It has a red face, red hair, and a fondness for alcohol, which are descriptions that fit the sculptor.

00:11:42.380 --> 00:11:43.040
*uuuh*

00:11:43.140 --> 00:11:45.660
Especially, as you'll see, in the next few facts.

00:11:52.900 --> 00:11:58.760
Later in the game, Emma leaves to tend to Kuro and Ishiin at the top of Ashina castle

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:06.420
And while she's gone there, during the siege of Ashina, the sculptor, too, takes this opportunity to leave.

00:12:06.420 --> 00:12:13.640
If you talk to the merchant here around this time, he mentions that the sculptor left, muttering something about... the flames.

00:12:13.640 --> 00:12:17.020
And past the corpses of Anayama and Kotaro,

00:12:17.020 --> 00:12:25.800
past this squadron of government soldiers, and past some red-hot claw marks, there is the demon of hatred, terrorizing the landscape.

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:27.520
This is Sekijo.

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:30.960
It's the sculptor, engulfed by Shura's wrath.

00:12:30.960 --> 00:12:34.840
So Sekiro, himself recognized the sculptor when I fought him,

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:37.980
which as I would come to realize is because I

00:12:38.500 --> 00:12:42.179
eavesdropped a lot and I shared a lot of sake which led to my character

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:44.699
figuring out who the demon of hatred is.

00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:53.160
If you don't do these things throughout the game, Sekiro does not recognize the demon of hatred, but the demon of hatred always recognizes you at the end.

00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:09.220
I hope you're preparing to cry over the next few weeks

00:13:09.700 --> 00:13:14.980
This old woman always was foreshadowing a demon appearing, because back then she asks:

00:13:15.120 --> 00:13:19.140
"Where do you think all that hatred from the war? Where do you think it goes?"

00:13:19.240 --> 00:13:26.020
And now, her dialogue here, at the end, depends on whether you knew the demon's identity this whole time.

00:13:26.020 --> 00:13:29.160
And, of course, now you do.

00:13:50.240 --> 00:13:55.920
I know! You're all aching for a lore video, and while I do have them in the works, trust me,

00:13:56.280 --> 00:14:01.379
I enjoy talking about the gameplay more right now, as you all wrap up your own playthroughs :)

00:14:01.390 --> 00:14:03.780
It's actually been a difficult last few months.

00:14:03.780 --> 00:14:07.229
I have to balance the needs of my firstborn child who was born in January,

00:14:07.229 --> 00:14:12.240
and I also have to balance the needs of YouTube, and Twitch, and also Teespring as well!

00:14:12.400 --> 00:14:14.040
So, thank you for being patient.

00:14:14.460 --> 00:14:20.060
Big thank you to all of you who actually bought a t-shirt over the last few weeks! It's doing really well!

00:14:20.070 --> 00:14:25.410
I didn't think anyone wanted merch, but now I'm at the point where I think I should actually work with an artist

00:14:25.510 --> 00:14:30.179
every month and throw a ton of money at them so that they can make cool designs for you guys!

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:35.250
Which, if you know me, you probably know that I dig that sort of stuff. I love it.

00:14:36.120 --> 00:14:40.180
And I'll see you next time. Remember to ring the bell if you want to be notified of new videos...

00:14:40.180 --> 00:14:41.500
And I'll see you then!

